  "body": "## What changed\n\n- Added `exit: Option<f64>` to `ThreadBore` in `crates/sim/src/verify/thread_bore.rs`.\n- Set `exit` to `h.through.then_some(h.floor_z)` in `thread_rims::thread_bores` (`crates/app/src/operation/thread_rims.rs`).\n- Added `ThreadBore::at_exit` so `wall_radius` excuses a through hole's exit face on the minor circle band when every vertex satisfies `z <= exit + WALL_BAND` and every minor-circle vertex satisfies `z >= exit - WALL_BAND`.\n- Required a present `exit` in `excused` to be finite and at or below `top`.\n- Added pinning tests in `crates/sim/src/verify/thread_bore.rs`, `crates/app/src/operation/thread_op.rs`, and `crates/app/tests/thread_mill_rim.rs`, and recorded the design decision in `docs/decisions/2655-thread-through-hole-gouge.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nOn a through hole, `machining2d::thread_mill` extends the helix one pitch below `floor_z` so the teeth finish the thread out of the bottom exit.\nThe cutter spans `floor_z` during the lead-in and helix moves, which meet the bottom face triangles on the hole's minor rim.\n`ThreadBore` previously knew only `top` (`entry_z`) and excused horizontal mouth facets only at `z >= top - WALL_BAND`.\nEvery bottom exit facet therefore returned `None` from `wall_radius`, and the solid law flagged each move with `Warning::Gouge` (\"move N cuts past the finish surface\").\n\n## Tests\n\n- Pins:\n  - `thread_mill_rim::a_detected_through_hole_with_tm0600_verifies_clean_and_posts`: failed before the fix with 21 `Gouge` warnings on lead-in and helix moves; passes after the fix with clean verify, empty verification gate, zero stock-sim gouge cells, and clean Fanuc post.\n  - `thread_mill_rim::a_through_hole_into_a_lower_part_still_convicts`: passes after the fix (a lower plate below the exit still convicts).\n  - `verify::thread_bore::tests::a_through_hole_exit_face_is_excused_while_blind_and_shelves_are_not`: passes after the fix (tests flat and sloped exits, blind holes, intermediate shelves, lower surfaces, inner steps, major radius limits, and non-finite or inverted `exit`).\n  - `operation::thread_op::tests::the_thread_grant_reads_the_threads_own_pitch_and_only_over_a_round_wall`: passes after the fix (verifies `exit` is `None` for blind holes and `Some(floor_z)` for through holes).\n- Mutation results:\n  - Restoring `crates/sim/src/verify/thread_bore.rs` and `crates/app/src/operation/thread_rims.rs` from `upstream/main`: `a_detected_through_hole_with_tm0600_verifies_clean_and_posts` failed with 21 `Gouge` warnings; restored -> passed.\n  - Removing the minor-circle lower bound (`p.z >= exit - WALL_BAND`) in `ThreadBore::at_exit`: `a_through_hole_exit_face_is_excused_while_blind_and_shelves_are_not` failed (`Some(5.0)` instead of `None` at `z = 9.0`); restored -> passed.\n  - Setting `exit: Some(h.floor_z)` unconditionally in `thread_rims::thread_bores`: `the_thread_grant_reads_the_threads_own_pitch_and_only_over_a_round_wall` failed (`Some(-10.0)` instead of `None` on a blind hole); restored -> passed.\n- Gate and clippy:\n  - `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 307 step(s), 0 failed (24.0 min).\n  - `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: passed with 0 warnings.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone (`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty).\n\n## Not exercised\n\nThe `batch` and `release` gate tiers (including `camcraft-kernel` and ignored release lanes) did not run on this branch; `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` and `cargo clippy` on `camcraft-sim` and `camcraft-app` covered the touched crates and mapped suites.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nNone.\n\nChangelog: Thread milling a detected through hole no longer reports false finish-surface gouges on its exit face, so it verifies clean and posts (#2655)\n\nFixes #2655\n",
